course: dictionary
lesson: 440
title: Words from history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a word. When you meet a new word, read the sentence and look for clues. «In June 1914, Archduke Franz Ferdinand was shot in Sarajevo, and within weeks most of Europe was at war.» The sentence does not say what an archduke is, but the clues are the war and the important name, so it must be a person of great importance.
explain: Look for the clues about royalty. «The heir to the throne of Austria-Hungary, Archduke Franz Ferdinand, was shot in Sarajevo.» An heir is the person who will rule next, and a throne belongs to a king or queen. So an archduke must belong to a royal family. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A very important prince fits, so that is your meaning.
explain: Now check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The heir to the throne of Austria-Hungary, a very important prince of the old royal family, was shot in Sarajevo.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. The word duke is inside archduke, and the dictionary tells you an archduke is a higher rank than a duke.
fact: «Archduke» means a very important prince in the old royal family of Austria.
fact: A woman with this rank is called an archduchess.
fact: The shooting of Archduke Franz Ferdinand in Sarajevo in 1914 led to the start of the First World War.
fact: An archduke has a higher rank than a duke.
fact: Clue words such as heir, throne and royal family can tell you that a word is about royalty.
exercise: «In June 1914, Archduke Franz Ferdinand was shot in Sarajevo.» What is an archduke? | A small town near a river | A soldier who fights at sea | *A very important prince in the old royal family of Austria | A kind of Scottish dinner
exercise: What is the word for a woman with this rank? | arcade | *archduchess | archway | archduke
exercise: «The heir to Austria-Hungary's throne, Archduke Franz Ferdinand, was shot in Sarajevo.» Which word is a clue that an archduke is royal? | shot | Sarajevo | June | *throne
test: «Within weeks most of Europe was at war.» What did the shooting of the archduke lead to? | The end of the old royal family | A new duke in Scotland | A holiday across Europe | *The start of the First World War
test: Which rank is higher? | *An archduke | A knight | A duke | They are both the same rank
exam: Ruth says an archduke is just a duke with a longer name. Why is she wrong? | Because they mean exactly the same, so she is right | *Because an archduke is a higher rank, a very important prince in the royal family | Because archduke is a Scottish word | Because only women can be archdukes
